## Basic

Drag in the area to set saturation and brightness, and use the slider to set the hue. The value is a CSS color string, such as `#0f62fe`. Bind to `value`, or listen for `input` while the color changes and `change` when a choice settles.

<FileSource src="/framed/ColorPicker/ColorPickerBound" />

## Format

Set `format` to `"hex"`, `"rgb"` or `"hsl"` to choose the text fields and how `value` is written: `#0f62fe`, `rgb(15, 98, 254)` or `hsl(219, 99%, 53%)`. The format switch under the sliders changes it, so bind `format` to follow the choice. A `value` in any of the three forms is read as is, and is not rewritten until the color changes.

### RGB

<ColorPicker format="rgb" value="rgb(15, 98, 254)" />

### HSL

<ColorPicker format="hsl" value="hsl(219, 99%, 53%)" />

## Alpha

Set `alpha` to add an alpha slider and field. The value gains an alpha part: `#0f62fe80` or `rgba(15, 98, 254, 0.5)`. Without `alpha`, `value` is always opaque and drops any alpha it was given.

<ColorPicker alpha format="rgb" value="rgba(15, 98, 254, 0.5)" />

## Swatches

Pass `swatches` to add a grid of preset colors. Give a swatch a `label` to name it for a screen reader; one without a label is named by color, as in "dark teal". Set `swatchColumns` for the number of swatches in a row.

<ColorPicker {swatches} value="#24a148" />

### Recent colors

The picker keeps the colors you chose last in `recent`, newest first, and shows them as a second row. A color is added when a pick settles: the end of a drag, a typed value, a swatch, the eyedropper, or focus leaving a control after the keyboard changed it. Bind `recent` to keep the list between visits, and set `recentLimit` to `0` to turn the row off.

<FileSource src="/framed/ColorPicker/ColorPickerRecent" />

## Contrast

Set `background` to the color the chosen color sits on, and the picker warns when the WCAG contrast ratio between them falls below `minContrast`, 4.5 by default. Use `3` for an icon or a border. A color with alpha is laid over the background first, and a background with alpha over white.

<FileSource src="/framed/ColorPicker/ColorPickerContrast" />

## Eyedropper

In browsers that have the EyeDropper API (Chromium), a button beside the preview picks any color on the screen. It is not rendered on the server or in other browsers, so the layout there has no gap for it. Set `hideEyeDropper` to remove it.

<ColorPicker hideEyeDropper />

## Text fields

Set `hideInputs` to hide the format switch and the text fields, as when a field of your own already shows the value.

<ColorPicker hideInputs />

## Disabled

Set `disabled` to `true` to prevent interaction.

<ColorPicker disabled {swatches} value="#0f62fe" />

## Read-only

Set `readonly` to `true` to show a color the user cannot change. The thumbs, fields and swatches stay focusable, and the eyedropper hides.

<ColorPicker readonly {swatches} value="#0f62fe" />

## Accessibility

The area is one slider with a role description of "2D slider". Its value text names both axes and the color, as in "Saturation 60%, brightness 40%, dark teal", so a screen reader user hears where the thumb is without seeing the area. Override the wording with `translateWithId`, and the color names with `formatColorName`.

| Key | Action |
| :-- | :-- |
| <DocKbd label="ArrowLeft" /> <DocKbd label="ArrowRight" /> | Change the saturation by 1. In a right-to-left layout, the keys swap. |
| <DocKbd label="ArrowUp" /> <DocKbd label="ArrowDown" /> | Change the brightness by 1. |
| <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + an arrow | Change the value by 10. |
| <DocKbd label="PageUp" /> <DocKbd label="PageDown" /> | Change the brightness by 10. |
| <DocKbd label="Home" /> <DocKbd label="End" /> | Set the saturation to its lowest or highest value. |
| <DocKbd label="Tab" /> | Move between the area, the hue slider, the alpha slider, the fields and the swatches. The swatches are one tab stop. |

The hue and alpha sliders take the same keys. The swatches are a listbox: the arrow keys move focus, and <DocKbd label="Enter" /> or <DocKbd label="Space" /> chooses, so moving through the swatches does not change the color on the way.

In a right-to-left layout the area, the sliders and the swatches mirror, and so does the hue, so the start of every track sits at the inline start. In forced colors mode, the area, the sliders, the preview and the swatches keep their colors, the fields show the value as text, and the chosen swatch carries a check mark.

| Do | Why |
| :-- | :-- |
| Show the value as text, beside or below the picker | The color in the area and preview is not available to everyone, and the text is what a form submits. |
| Set `background` where the color is text or an icon | The warning is the only cue that a color is too faint to read. |
| Label each swatch | A name such as "Blue 60" says more than a color name does. |
